        "original_id": "51566d86-92c4-5967-a207-811eafea72d8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Luis Gianneo, Ariel Ramírez, Juan Carlos Zorzi, Virtú Maragno, Pedro Ignacio Calderón, Rodolfo Arizaga\n- Roles: music educator, composer, pianist, music director\n- Topics: Argentine folk music, music education\n\nFacts:\n- Luis Gianneo was a music educator who taught composers Ariel Ramírez, Juan Carlos Zorzi, Virtú Maragno, Pedro Ignacio Calderón, and Rodolfo Arizaga, among others.\n- Ariel Ramírez was born on 4 September 1921.\n- Ariel Ramírez was an Argentine composer, pianist, and music director.\n- Ariel Ramírez was considered a chief exponent of Argentine folk music and was noted for his iconic musical compositions.\n- Ariel Ramírez died on 18 February 2010.",
